  "worked_solution": "First, since $s=10t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{10}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{10}) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{s}{10})\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{6s}{10})j+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{6s}{10})k \\\\  & =\\frac{4s}{5}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3s}{5})k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4s}{5})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3s}{5}))j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3s}{5}))k \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3s}{5})k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
